Atoms that tie on tier, conditions and cover are ordered by their rule
text, so adding an unrelated input file does not change the order of the
rules of another file.

  $ cat > use.ml <<EOT
  > [@@@css.atoms [
  >   ("_small", ["@media (min-width:600px){._small{color:red;}}"], 2, 1, 1, []);
  >   ("_large", ["@media (min-width:900px){._large{color:blue;}}"], 2, 1, 1, [])
  > ]]
  > EOT

  $ cat > aside.ml <<EOT
  > [@@@css.atoms [
  >   ("_large", ["@media (min-width:900px){._large{color:blue;}}"], 2, 1, 1, [])
  > ]]
  > EOT

  $ styled-ppx.generate use.ml
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  @media (min-width:600px){._small{color:red;}}
  @media (min-width:900px){._large{color:blue;}}
  $ styled-ppx.generate aside.ml use.ml
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  @media (min-width:600px){._small{color:red;}}
  @media (min-width:900px){._large{color:blue;}}
